L.append("# DECLARED (THE LEAN PASS, owner-ruled 2026-09-23 — DEUTERONOMY_WALK.md \"THE LEAN PASS\"; the state doc's #208): NO DOCKET at this sitting — the testing shelf's cases are THE MISHNAH ROWS THE READING'S LEDGER CITES AT LEAST TWICE (logic/oral_triage/deu_19_21_shoftim_ki_teitzei_2026-09-24.md — the rows' citations counted by the regex: %d distinct Mishnah citations, %d cited at least twice; the three CITED IN THE SPINE'S OWN HEBREW among them at 181:1 (Makkot 2:8), 205:1 (Sotah 9:9) and 206:1 (Sotah 9:2) — %s), TWENTY-EIGHT rows: %s — each read WHOLE from the export (Data/sefaria_export/Mishnah_<tractate>/he.json and en.json, chapter:paragraph), Hebrew and English, at the design (the whole-row rule, owner-ruled 2026-09-17; ch19_exam_rows.py printed them whole, 65,637 characters), each a case of a cell of cold_run_refuge_war_family.py with its verdict a DATA row or a PARAMETER (the code/data separation law: the Mishnah's rows fed at run time, never written into the source). A TALMUD SEGMENT only where a Mishnah verdict is disputed and a cell needs it: NONE READ — the disputed rows (Makkot 2:8's rent and office, Makkot 2:7's beyond the boundary, Sotah 9:1's three or five, Parah 1:1's one year or two, Sanhedrin 6:4's who is hanged and the beam, Sanhedrin 8:2's measures, Sotah 8:5's fearful) carry the arms on the Mishnah's own line and the cells record them all. THE FULL DOCKET OWED to the full process (COMPILE_DEBT.md's lean-pass box): Makkot 1-2; Sotah 8-9; Sanhedrin 6, 8-9; Bava Batra 8; Bekhorot 8; Yevamot 4; Parah 1; Negaim 2; Shevuot 5; the segments Makkot 5a-7a, 9b-13a, Sotah 42a-47b, Sanhedrin 45a-47b, 68b-72a, Bava Batra 122b-124b, Bekhorot 46a-52b, Kiddushin 21b-22a, Yevamot 48a, Bava Kamma 91b, Shabbat 19a." % (len(cites), len(TWICE), ', '.join('%s %d:%d' % k for k in HEB), ', '.join('%s %d:%d' % (t, c, p) for t, c, p in TWICE)))
L.append("# THE VERDICTS: LAW names the cell and the ask of cold_run_refuge_war_family.py that grades the row (F1 the_cities_of_refuge, F2 the_landmark_and_the_witnesses, F3 the_priests_speech, F5 the_broken_necked_heifer, F7 the_firstborns_double, F8 the_rebellious_son, F9 the_hanged); the row's own words the case, the verdict the arms the Mishnah records; the ledger's citing rows COMPUTED per Mishnah row. The Mishnah's rows by chapter:paragraph (the export's index).")
L.append("# COVERAGE (computed): %d of %d declared rows read whole (Hebrew %d, English %d); segments read 0; rows outside the chapters' verses 0 (Bekhorot 8:1's redemption from the priest, Sotah 9:9's bitter waters and clusters, Sanhedrin 8:5's wine and sleep, Parah 1:1's red cow, vineyard and afflicted house the rows' other clauses — each row read whole as the rule requires)." % (len(read), len(ROWS), sum(1 for r in read if r[3]), sum(1 for r in read if r[4])))
L.append("")
L.append("## THE TWENTY-EIGHT ROWS (each read whole; the verdict beside it; the ledger's citing rows computed)")
for (tr, c, p, he, en), (tr_, c_, p_, vs, cell, opening) in zip(read, ROWS):
    L.append("- Mishnah %s %d:%d — LAW. On %s; cited by the ledger's rows %s (%d citations). THE ROW (English, whole): %s THE HEBREW OPENS: %s. THE CELL: %s." % (tr, c, p, vs, ', '.join(WHERE[(tr, c, p)]), cites[(tr, str(c), str(p))], en, opening, cell))
L.append("")
L.append("## CITE INDEX — every source opened, each fully named")
for tr, c, p, he, en in read:
    L.append("- Mishnah %s %d:%d (Data/sefaria_export/Mishnah_%s/he.json and en.json — chapter %d, paragraph %d; read whole)" % (tr, c, p, tr.replace(' ', '_'), c, p))
text = '\n'.join(L) + '\n'
open(OUT, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(text)
print('THE LEAN EXAM WRITTEN: %s — %d bytes; %d rows read whole (%d cited in the Hebrew: %s); segments read 0; the ledger\'s distinct citations %d' % (OUT, len(text.encode()), len(read), len(HEB), HEB, len(cites)))
